Reactor licensing scope
=======================

This repository contains separately licensed projects. The following scope
notices do not modify the complete license texts referenced below.

1. Donald Microduck

   Software retains the official upstream Apache-2.0 license in
   donald-microduck/LICENSE. Upstream and derived model assets retain the
   original noncommercial, share-alike notice in
   donald-microduck/UPSTREAM_LICENSES.md.

2. Mickey Hub

   First-party designs, models, documentation and media use Creative Commons
   Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International (CC BY-NC 4.0).

   First-party firmware and software tools use the PolyForm Noncommercial
   License 1.0.0.

   The complete, unmodified texts are in mickeyhub/LICENSES/. See
   mickeyhub/LICENSE for scope and third-party exclusions.

3. Commercial production and authorization

   Noncommercial development, sharing, personal builds and prototypes are
   available under the applicable public licenses and their conditions.
   Commercial manufacture, commissioned production for sale, and other
   commercial uses outside those permissions require a separate written
   commercial license from the relevant rights holders before they begin.
   There is no production-volume exemption. Publishing source or design
   files does not waive the noncommercial conditions.

   Contact the Reactor maintainers at phyreact@gmail.com to request
   authorization. A request alone is not permission.

4. Shared Reactor material

   Original shared documentation and graphics use CC BY-NC 4.0, whose full
   text is in mickeyhub/LICENSES/CC-BY-NC-4.0.txt. Shared artwork, models and
   scenes retain the terms of incorporated assets, including Microduck's
   upstream share-alike condition.

5. Third-party material

   Original third-party licenses and explicit file-level notices take
   precedence for the works they identify. No third-party rights are
   relicensed here. A Reactor commercial authorization can grant only rights
   held or controlled by its grantor.

See LICENSING.md and THIRD_PARTY.md for project scope and source information.
